      "v": 4,
      "zh": "既 是 這 樣 ， 你 們 若 有 今 生 的 事 當 審 判 ， 是 派 教 會 所 輕 看 的 人 審 判 麼 ？",
      "en": "So if you have ordinary lawsuits, do you appoint as judges those who have no standing in the church?[NOTE:1]",
      "notes": [
        "Or “if you have ordinary lawsuits, appoint as judges those who have no standing in the church!” This alternative reading (cf. KJV, NIV84) takes the Greek verb καθίζετε (kathizete) as an ironic imperative instead of a question. This verb comes, however, at the end of the sentence. It is not impossible that Paul meant for it to be understood this way, but its placement in the sentence does not make this probable. NIV11 renders the phrase as a question “do you ask for a ruling from those whose way of life is scorned in the church?”"
